              "[{'generated_text': \"Hi, I love AI and ML!\\n\\nI'm an electrical engineer with a PhD in Applied Physics.\\n\\nI'm interested in AI and Machine Learning applications in the field of Electrical Engineering.\\n\\nI have a keen interest in machine learning and its applications to various fields, especially in the field of engineering. I'm particularly interested in developing solutions for difficult problems related to the field of electrical engineering.\\n\\nI have a background in computer science and mathematics, and I have a keen interest in AI and machine learning. I have worked on various AI and ML-based projects in the past. I have a strong interest in developing solutions for difficult problems related to the field of electrical engineering. I have a keen interest in developing solutions for difficult problems related to the field of electrical engineering.\\n\\nMy research interests include machine learning, AI, natural language processing, computer vision and robotics. I have a background in electrical engineering and have worked on many projects related to these areas.\\n\\nI am an Electrical Engineer with a PhD in Applied Physics and a Master's degree in Electrical Engineering. I am passionate about developing solutions that can help solve complex problems in the field of electrical engineering. I have worked on various projects related to electrical engineering and have developed solutions that have helped to make a difference in the field.\"},\n",
              " {'generated_text': \"Hi, I love AI and ML, I'm working on a project where I'm trying to put these things together.\\n\\nI believe I'm going to do some classification and want to make a prediction based on the number I see after the prediction, but I'm stuck with the data and how to make a prediction.\\n\\nIf I have 1000 numbers and I want to predict the number that will be most likely based on the numbers I see, how I go about doing that?\\n\\n• I just realized that your question asks something completely different from the way I have interpreted it. You're asking for an algorithm that can predict the next number in a sequence. This is something that can be done with an algorithm that can learn from a sequence of numbers. I'll try to clarify the question in a few days. –\\xa0Erik Pjorts Jan 20 at 14:16\\n• @ErikPjorts Thanks, I'm still trying to understand your answer. –\\xa0user163158 Jan 20 at 15:16\\n\\n## 2 Answers\\n\\nYou should be able to use a simple neural network with a single hidden layer to perform this task. The input layer should have one number (\"}]"
